  "details": "1. Enter world https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_8283d83d-9a45-43d1-8a6f-b4b7488c5300\n\n2. Click the shuffle button\n\n3. Scale your avatar so your eye height is around 1.73 meters\n\n4. Attempt to pick up tiles\n\nExpected behavior: The tile highlighted should generally be the one closest to your hand.\n\nActual behavior:\n\nThe tile highlighted appears somewhat random. In some cases, you can't pick up a tile even if the tile is right near your hand.\n\nVideo demonstrating the issue: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EvXkofzdx0s\n\nI've included a debug UI to change the proximity settings of the tiles; it doesn't help, but it does show that the broken behavior is not proximity dependent.\n\nI'm not sure when this regressed, but possible somewhere around the time when all the proximity-related changes went in.\n\nNote also that with avatar height below 1.19m, pickups are more well-behaved.",
